        438.1195373535156,
        333.2298889160156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "tgt",
      "bbox": [
        434.52801513671875,
        330.4359436035156,
        443.32000732421875,
        334.8593444824219
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "vϵ(x) > 0.",
      "bbox": [
        445.4730224609375,
        318.0719299316406,
        488.6115417480469,
        327.8328552246094
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We will use the above assumptions to ensure uniform",
      "bbox": [
        323.16302490234375,
        342.3873291015625,
        558.0015258789062,
        351.29388427734375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "energy decrease toward the target energy band and repeated",
      "bbox": [
        313.20001220703125,
        354.3423156738281,
        558.0010375976562,
        363.2488708496094
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "opportunities to apply control through recurrence of the",
      "bbox": [
        313.20001220703125,
        366.29730224609375,
        558.0007934570312,
        375.203857421875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "zero-input dynamics. Once the trajectory reaches this energy",
      "bbox": [
        313.20001220703125,
        378.2522888183594,
        558.0010375976562,
        387.1588439941406
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "band, the ergodic structure of the Hamiltonian flow ensures",
      "bbox": [
        313.20001220703125,
        390.2082824707031,
        558.0009155273438,
        399.1148376464844
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "eventual arrival to the target set.",
      "bbox": [
        313.20001220703125,
        402.16326904296875,
        445.48333740234375,
        411.06982421875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Theorem 2 (Target Reachability). Consider system (1) under",
      "bbox": [
        313.20001220703125,
        419.7406921386719,
        558.001220703125,
        428.7668151855469
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Assumptions 1–5. Let K = {(xi, ri, ui)}N",
      "bbox": [
        313.20001220703125,
        430.1150817871094,
        499.27227783203125,
        441.4167785644531
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "i=1 be a finite",
      "bbox": [
        492.96099853515625,
        431.9049377441406,
        557.9979858398438,
        443.085693359375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "assignment set. Assume that K satisfies the following:",
      "bbox": [
        313.20001220703125,
        443.0529479980469,
        534.3596801757812,
        452.4576416015625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "1) Local energy decrease: For each (xi, ri, ui) ∈K,",
      "bbox": [
        313.20001220703125,
        456.0059509277344,
        531.457275390625,
        466.3258056640625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "∆H(xi(τi))+v0τi+LHrieLτi ≤∆H(xi)−LHri,",
      "bbox": [
        341.37896728515625,
        471.5689392089844,
        543.103515625,
        485.0047912597656
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "where xi(τi) := ϕ(τi, xi, ui), τmin = mini τi, and v0>0.",
      "bbox": [
        326.47991943359375,
        493.9238586425781,
        558.0017700195312,
        504.2646179199219
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "2) Energy coverage: Let c := supx∈S0 ∆H(x). Then",
      "bbox": [
        313.19989013671875,
        505.6428527832031,
        532.2650146484375,
        517.921630859375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "∆H(x) ≤c",
      "bbox": [
        355.7268981933594,
        523.7649536132812,
        404.16510009765625,
        533.1696166992188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "=⇒",
      "bbox": [
        412.4639587402344,
        523.7649536132812,
        428.5137023925781,
        533.1696166992188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "H(x) ∈H(Supp(K)).",
      "bbox": [
        436.822509765625,
        523.7649536132812,
        528.7872924804688,
        533.1696166992188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "3) Ergodic coverage: For all E ∈H(Supp(K)) and all",
      "bbox": [
        313.19989013671875,
        542.2099609375,
        558.0208129882812,
        551.7640380859375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ergodic components KE",
      "bbox": [
        326.4798889160156,
        553.1820068359375,
        426.13690185546875,
        563.5696411132812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "α ⊆ΣE,",
      "bbox": [
        419.5728759765625,
        554.1649780273438,
        456.7155456542969,
        566.0325927734375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "int(Supp(K)) ∩KE",
      "bbox": [
        389.60089111328125,
        571.363037109375,
        472.9669189453125,
        582.2496337890625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "α̸ = ∅.",
      "bbox": [
        466.4039001464844,
        572.844970703125,
        494.8852844238281,
        584.712646484375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Then, the chain policy πK ensures that for almost every",
      "bbox": [
        323.1618957519531,
        591.8468017578125,
        558.004150390625,
        602.1786499023438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "x0 ∈S0, there exists t < ∞such that",
      "bbox": [
        313.19989013671875,
        603.2439575195312,
        468.5482482910156,
        614.1436157226562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ϕ(t, x0, πK) ∈Stgt.",
      "bbox": [
        395.44189453125,
        621.9239501953125,
        475.7594909667969,
        632.2437744140625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Proof. We first establish three key points: (i) each control",
      "bbox": [
        313.19989013671875,
        641.0863037109375,
        558.0009155273438,
        649.9928588867188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "segment decreases the energy distance on its associated",
      "bbox": [
        313.19989013671875,
        653.041259765625,
        558.0007934570312,
        661.9478149414062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "support ball, (ii) whenever the trajectory leaves the support,",
      "bbox": [
        313.19989013671875,
        664.9962768554688,
        558.0008544921875,
        673.90283203125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the zero-input dynamics return it to the support in finite time",
      "bbox": [
        313.19989013671875,
        676.9512939453125,
        558.0007934570312,
        685.8578491210938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "for almost every initial condition, and (iii) once the trajectory",
      "bbox": [
        313.19989013671875,
        688.90625,
        558.000732421875,
        697.8128051757812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "enters the target energy band, it reaches the target set in finite",
      "bbox": [
        313.19989013671875,
        700.8612670898438,
        558.000732421875,
        709.767822265625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "time for almost every initial condition. We then combine",
      "bbox": [
        313.19989013671875,
        712.8172607421875,
        558.0008544921875,
        721.7238159179688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "these three arguments to conclude the theorem.",
      "bbox": [
        313.19989013671875,
        724.7722778320312,
        506.86279296875,
        733.6788330078125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    }
